# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
/target/

# Private target dir for the r16-r2 activity line. Another line builds the shared
# `target/` on this machine at the same time, so this worktree redirects
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR here (see docs/activity-storage.md §5.2); without this line
# `git status` would offer to track ~GBs of artifacts.
/target-r2/

# Generated by Tauri
# will have schema files for capabilities auto-completion
/gen/schemas

# Private target dir for the round-16 final verification. The shared `target/` is
# held by a concurrent line on this machine (see /target-r2/ above), and a build that
# only queues behind someone else's lock is a wait, not a verification.
/target-r16f/

# Same reason, r18: another line on this box held the shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` lock
# while this one needed `cargo test --lib`, so the three Rust directions of this round
# build under CARGO_TARGET_DIR=…/src-tauri/target-r18mine. Measured cost of the switch:
# one full dependency build; every later run in the same directory is incremental.
/target-r18mine/
